## Conventions (short reminder; full text in `WIKI_SCHEMA.md`)

- **Concept vs Entity.** Concept = a generalisable idea (Sharpe Ratio,
  Compound Interest). Entity = a proper noun (Acme Corp, Alice). When in
  doubt → entity.
- **File names** use canonical name verbatim (`Sharpe Ratio.md`).
  `_sources/` slugs are kebab-case.
- **Every fact** on a concept/entity page must end with a `[^src-<slug>]`
  footnote. No footnote → don't add the fact. This is the audit trail.
- **Additivity.** Ingest never silently overwrites prior facts. Conflict →
  insert a `## Contradictions` block, escalate to the operator.
- **One page, one place.** A given concept/entity lives in exactly one
  layer (course-local OR root-shared). Maintained by promote/demote.
- **`_sources/` is never promoted.** A source belongs to where it was
  ingested.
- **`log.md` is append-only.** Past entries are part of the audit trail —
  never edit them retroactively.

---

## The human's job, the LLM's job

Per the Karpathy pattern:

- **You curate** which sources to ingest, **direct** the analysis, **ask
  good questions**, **resolve contradictions**.
- **Claude does** the bookkeeping — summarising, cross-referencing, filing,
  updating 10–15 pages per ingest, maintaining `index.md` and `log.md`,
  suggesting follow-up questions during `lint`.

The LLM does not get bored, does not forget to update a cross-reference,
and can touch 15 files in one pass. That is why a wiki of this size stays
maintained.

